        "original_id": "32f243ee-8daa-51a2-9e7c-c5f7f5cff1d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rumi, Farouk El-Baz\n- Roles: poet, jurist, Islamic scholar, theologian, Sufi mystic, space scientist\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Projects: Apollo missions\n- Topics: Persian literature, Sunni Islam, Sufism, lunar exploration\n\nFacts:\n- Rumi, also known as Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Rūmī, Jalāl ad-Dīn Muhammad Balkhī, Mevlânâ/Mawlānā, and Mevlevî/Mawlawī, was born on 30 September 1207 and died on 17 December 1273.\n- Rumi was a 13th-century Persian Sunni Muslim poet, jurist, Islamic scholar, theologian, and Sufi mystic.\n- Farouk El-Baz was born on January 2, 1938.\n- Farouk El-Baz is an Egyptian American space scientist.\n- Farouk El-Baz worked with NASA on planning scientific exploration of the Moon.\n- Farouk El-Baz helped select landing sites for the Apollo missions and trained astronauts in lunar observations and photography.",
